# Technical Writing Style Guide for Persian (Right-to-Left / RTL)

Use these rules whenever writing Persian technical documentation or bilingual answers (AI, ML, software engineering, systems design). English-only replies are unchanged.

---

## 1. Visual Layout & RTL Alignment

* **Markdown Table Alignment:** Right-align columns with colons on the right (`|---:|`). Prevents LTR default column alignment.
* **Text Diagrams & Flowcharts:** Reverse flow arrows to RTL (`←` instead of `→`).
* **Persian Numerals:** Use Eastern Arabic numerals (`۰۱۲۳۴۵۶۷۸۹`) in general prose, ordered steps, and metrics inside Persian text. Keep Western digits (`0123456789`) only in code, paths, equations, and raw variable names.
* **Persian Punctuation:**
  * Comma: `،` (not `,`)
  * Question mark: `؟` (not `?`)
  * Quotes: « » (not `" "`)

---

## 2. English Code Terms & Mixed Text

* Wrap variables, schemas, decorators, files, and paths in backticks (e.g. `continue_research`, `checkpoints.sqlite3`, `@strategy(PREDICT)`).
* Never start a sentence or bullet with an English word. Lead with Persian (or the bullet) so RTL orientation is anchored before inline code.
* Keep domain acronyms in English uppercase: API, LLM, JSON, UI, ML, SQLite, CV — do not transliterate them.

---

## 3. Specialized Technical Glossary

Prefer industry-standard Iranian SE/AI terms; avoid literal calques:

| English | Recommended Persian | Avoid |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Orchestrator | ارکستراتور / مدیریت اجرا | هماهنگ‌کننده |
| Data Leakage | نشت داده | فرار اطلاعات |
| Checkpoint | نقطهٔ بررسی / چک‌پوینت | نقطه بازرسی |
| Persistence | ماندگاری داده‌ها / پایداری | ایستایی |
| Subprocess | زیرپردازش / ساب‌پراسس | فرآیند فرعی |
| Holdout Data | داده‌های ارزیابی نهایی (Holdout) | داده‌های نگه‌داشته‌شده |
| Pipeline | پایپ‌لاین / زنجیرهٔ پردازش | مجرا / لوله |
| Deterministic | قطعی / قطعی‌نگر | تعیین‌شده |
| Agent | عامل / عامل هوشمند | نماینده / نماینده متحرک |

---

## 4. Typography & Grammar

* **ZWNJ (نیم‌فاصله):** Always — `می‌شود` (not `می شود`)، `عامل‌ها` (not `عامل ها`)، `پایگاه‌داده`، `پیش‌فرض`.
* **SOV order:** Subject–Object–Verb. Do not mirror English passive mid-sentence verb placement.
* **Tone:** Formal, objective, technical. Not chatty; not archaic.

---

## 5. QA Checklist (before finishing Persian docs)

1. Tables right-aligned (`|---:|`)?
2. Diagram arrows RTL (`←`)?
3. Prose numbers Persian (`۱، ۲، ۳`)?
4. Code/paths in backticks?
5. ZWNJ on `می‌` and `ها`?
6. Sentences end with a Persian verb?
